    "status": "present",
    "value": "Count paths from node1 to node n whose successive nodes have strictly decreasing shortest-path distance to n, modulo1000000007. The approach is: Dijkstra from final node followed by increasing-distance DAG path counting. Its target cost is O((n+e) log n) time/O(n+e) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
